# Test: NaCl RMP2 / LANL2DZ-ECP analytical Hessian and frequencies (v0.65.0)
#
# Diatomic with effective core potentials on BOTH atoms (Na: 10-electron
# core via LANL2; Cl: 10-electron core via LANL2).  Validates that the
# MP2 Hessian extension correctly handles the ECP gradient term in the
# inner compute_mp2_gradient (which dispatches on mol%necp > 0 to invoke
# ecp_gradient_analytical_md at every FD step).
#
# Starting from R(Na-Cl) = 2.36 A (close to MP2 minimum).
# Expected: 1 vibrational mode around 360 cm^-1 (experiment 363 cm^-1
# for gas-phase NaCl).
#
%method  MP2
%basis   LANL2DZ
%ecp     LANL2DZ
%frozen_core 0
%job     freq
%charge  0
%mult    1
%print_time

*geometry angstrom
Na   0.000   0.000   0.000
Cl   0.000   0.000   2.360
*end
